/*
	RMSTEST 9 — Test 7 again, with the actor area MADE VISIBLE.

	Test 7 was under-specified: an actor area is invisible, so "gold sat
	off-centre" could have meant "gold avoided the area" or "the area is not
	where I assumed and gold went where it liked". This marks the area with
	terrain, which costs nothing because terrain does not occupy tiles.

	THE MARKER
	  create_land DIRT at land_position 50 50 with base_size 5 stamps an 11x11
	  square. create_actor_area 60 60 1234 5 is a square radius in TILES
	  (guide:1994), so it covers 55..65 — the same 11x11.
	  The DIRT square therefore IS the actor area, drawn on the ground.
	  The GRASS land underneath is base_size 7 (15x15, spanning 53..67), so a
	  2-tile grass border remains visible around the dirt.

	This also silently checks a spec assumption: preview-design Sec.4 maps
	land_position 50 50 to tile round(50/100 * 120) = (60,60). If the dirt
	square is NOT concentric with the grass border, that mapping is wrong and
	is worth more than this test is.

	NO REFERENCE FRAME, deliberately. Tests 7 and 8 both showed
	place_on_specific_land_id does not confine the candidate set to that land,
	and here a frame would be actively harmful: the DIRT stamp takes ownership
	of the middle tiles, so a land-id frame could exclude the actor area for
	the wrong reason and fake a per-member result. Frameless gold is confined
	to the clearings anyway, because tree occupancy blocks the surrounding
	forest. set_gaia_object_only is omitted for the same reason it is not
	needed: guide:2354 scopes that requirement to per-player placement, and
	Test 3 confirmed it only under a frame.

	READ IT LIKE THIS
	  Gold sitting ON the dirt square
	      -> avoid_actor_area is NOT checked during the fill. Combined with
	         Test 8 (terrain_to_place_on also unchecked), tight grouping is
	         confirmed as a single uniform rule: the anchor is checked, the
	         fill is not, full stop.
	  Gold strictly on the 2-tile grass border, dirt square completely clear
	      -> avoid_actor_area IS checked per member, making it the one
	         exception to the rule Test 8 established. Sec.6.6 would then need
	         a genuine per-attribute distinction after all — for this attribute
	         only, and now with evidence rather than a guide inference.
	  No gold anywhere across several seeds
	      -> frameless gold needs something this map does not give it. Check
	         the STONE control: if stone also fails, the frameless assumption
	         above is wrong and I will re-do this with a frame plus a shared
	         land_id.

	The single STONE is the CONTROL: frameless, no avoidance. It must appear.

	RUN ON: Tiny, 2 players. One clearing at map centre, one sample per seed.
	Worth 3 or 4 seeds — Test 7 only produced gold about half the time.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain FOREST

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type DESERT
	base_size 3
	number_of_tiles 1
	circle_radius 45 0
}

/* The clearing: 15x15 grass, spans tiles 53..67. */
create_land
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	land_position 50 50
	base_size 7
	number_of_tiles 1
	land_id 5
	zone 7
}

/* The marker: 11x11 dirt, spans 55..65, stamped last so it stays visible
   (guide: "the land placed last will be the one visible"). Geometrically
   identical to the actor area declared below. */
create_land
{
	terrain_type DIRT
	land_position 50 50
	base_size 5
	number_of_tiles 1
	land_id 6
	zone 8
}

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

create_actor_area 60 60 1234 5

/* THE TEST: tight group that must avoid the (now visible) actor area. */
create_object GOLD
{
	number_of_objects 25
	set_tight_grouping
	avoid_actor_area 1234
}

/* CONTROL: no avoidance. Must appear. */
create_object STONE
{
	number_of_objects 1
}
